   "widgets_values": [
    "## 3: Video to character in one graph\n\nWorkflows 1 and 2 in one run: a side-view video of a person in, the move fitted to your character as a SCAIL cylinder pose video out. Use it for a quick try; once you fit one move to several characters, the two separate workflows save the scan time.\n\n1. **Load Video**: one person seen from the side, whole body in frame, static camera. Example: `sprint_kicks_side_720p.mp4` from the pack's `example_inputs/` (CC BY 3.0, see `ATTRIBUTION.md`), copied into `ComfyUI/input/`. Every 2nd frame, 81 frames.\n2. **Scan Video Poses** (DWPose with the feet, about 1 s per frame on a CPU) -> **Repair Pose Scan** -> **Track from Pose Scan** (*one-shot* for a move in place, *walk cycle* for a walk). **Preview Skeleton Track** plays the poses: orange = near limbs, blue = far, green dot = planted foot. **Save Skeleton Track** keeps the track for workflow 2.\n3. **Load Image**: your character, 768 x 1024, side view facing right, whole body, on white. Example: `cop_on_white.png` (or `mannequin_on_white.png`) from `example_inputs/`.\n4. **DWPose Estimator** -> **Fit Track to Character**: every bone keeps its direction per frame and takes the character's length. Check *Fit check* and the second preview.\n5. **Render SCAIL Cylinders** -> the pose video (mp4) and frames for SCAIL-Preview, z-buffered so the near limbs stay in front."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
